  "_id": "6a7f5797757ee51246381c55",
  "lab": "6a7f5796eda1a5feaff0b458",
  "name": "Rubella -IgM",
  "code": "RUBIM",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Rubella Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>IgG Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgG antibodies indicates past immunity to rubella. It suggests that the person has been previously infected with the rubella virus or has received the rubella vaccine. Immunity to future rubella infections is usually provided.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgM antibodies suggests a recent or current rubella infection. It indicates an ongoing or recent infection. Additional testing and clinical assessment are necessary to confirm the diagnosis.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>Simultaneous presence of both IgG and IgM antibodies may indicate a recent rubella infection or a recent rubella vaccination. Further evaluation is required to determine the specific stage and nature of the infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for both IgG and IgM antibodies indicates no current or previous exposure to rubella and no immunity to the virus. It means the person is susceptible to rubella infection.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
